' 24 The set: a receive takes a class, and a send retires a class.
'
' Source of Figure N11.9 in ../design.md (section N11.9). The figure restates
' the set plans of rholang/src/rust/interpreter/spaces/disciplines/scan.rs with
' the class key of spaces/disciplines/set.rs. It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order:
'   1. A receive takes the first record in the pick order of the operation
'      that its pattern binds. The guard is checked once, on the first member
'      of its class in DR-75 order.
'   2. A receive that does not peek fires one consume over [D] with the first
'      member of the class in DR-75 order and dispatches it. K_retire then
'      retires the other non-persistent members. A peek binds the record of
'      its pick alone, and RESTORE-SCAN sends it again (Rule E).
'   3. A send fires the first waiter in the pick order of the send that binds
'      and admits its datum. After a fire of a waiter that does not peek,
'      RETIRE-CLASS retires the stored non-persistent members of the class
'      with K_retire COMMs.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 24-set-class-fire.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 24-set-class-fire
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_note_amber
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title The set (P5a): a receive takes a class, and a send retires a class

start
if (the operation?) then (receive)
  :r ← the first record in the pick order of the receive
  whose payload the pattern binds; <<$rrs_agent>>
  if (a record r was found and the guard admits it?) then (yes)
    if (the receive peeks?) then (yes)
      :fire on [D] with r alone,
      then RESTORE-SCAN sends r again (Rule E); <<$rrs_flow>>
    else (no)
      :C ← every stored member of the class of r, in DR-75 order,
      one consume over [D] with the first member of C, which the
      outcome dispatches, and one K_retire COMM over [D] for each
      other non-persistent member of C; <<$rrs_effect>>
    endif
  else (no)
    :park the receive (the guard is checked once); <<$rrs_storage>>
  endif
else (send)
  :W ← the first waiter in the pick order of the send
  whose pattern binds the datum x and whose guard admits it; <<$rrs_agent>>
  if (a waiter W was found?) then (yes)
    :fire W with x; <<$rrs_effect>>
    if (W peeks?) then (no)
      :RETIRE-CLASS: one single-channel K_retire COMM for each
      stored non-persistent member of the class of x; <<$rrs_fail>>
    else (yes)
    endif
  else (no)
    :store x; <<$rrs_storage>>
  endif
endif
stop

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_agent>    | a choice of the plan, in the pick order of the operation |
|<$rrs_effect>   | a staged fire |
|<$rrs_flow>     | a second send (Rule E) |
|<$rrs_fail>     | the retire of the other members of a class |
|<$rrs_storage>  | a stored record or a parked waiter |
endlegend
@enduml
